# The step of the map scale_1, an array of one limb times a scalar of T (milestone2.md, "sum, dot,
# axpy, convolution"): the product rounded to nearest, mul_1_1. The program supplies both; a
# product needs no guard (rule R3). Its claims are those of mul_1_1.
kernel:        scale_step_1
input:         x
input:         a
output:        z
value:         x*a
ensures:       rounded z nearest
ensures:       error z R c=1/(1+u) k=1 t=1/2
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v scale_step_1_correct
ieee_bridge_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v scale_step_1_ieee_bridge
ieee_lead_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v scale_step_1_ieee_lead
source:        mul_1_1, one rounding to nearest
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
ieee:          bridge

z = mul_1_1(x, a)
